\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The radii that decide which centres cut $V_c$, in a plane through $c$, to scale. A centre $y$ cuts $V_c$ along the bisector $\langle x,y/|y|\rangle =|y|/2$. A contact, $|y|=2$, gives a facet tangent to the unit ball; a centre with $2<|y|<\sqrt  6$ cuts a cap off the ball $B(\sqrt  {3/2})$, which is where \cref  {lem:no-triple} measures the cell; at $|y|=\sqrt  6$ the bisector is tangent to $B(\sqrt  {3/2})$, and at $|y|=2\sqrt  2$ to $B(\sqrt  2)$, the ball circumscribed about the $24$-cell (\cref  {lem:shell-new}).}}{12}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
