\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The certificates on which proofs rest. The degree of a kernel on pairs with a distance label is given in the angle and in the distance; a semicolon separates the kernel on pairs from the kernel on typed triples. The last column gives the value that the certificate proves and the value that the theorem needs. In the first row the bound on the size of a code is exactly $24$, as the classification needs. In the next four rows the certificate proves a lower bound, which has to exceed the number on the right; for \cref  {thm:m23-labelled} it is the sign of every term of its proof. In the remaining rows it proves an upper bound, on $U(Y)$ or, in the last row, on the function $\Phi $ of the proof of \cref  {thm:cap-inequality}, which has to lie below the number on the right. For \cref  {thm:count30,prop:C-radial} the value is the largest over the cases of the proof.}}{20}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:certificates}{{1}{20}{The certificates on which proofs rest. The degree of a kernel on pairs with a distance label is given in the angle and in the distance; a semicolon separates the kernel on pairs from the kernel on typed triples. The last column gives the value that the certificate proves and the value that the theorem needs. In the first row the bound on the size of a code is exactly $24$, as the classification needs. In the next four rows the certificate proves a lower bound, which has to exceed the number on the right; for \cref {thm:m23-labelled} it is the sign of every term of its proof. In the remaining rows it proves an upper bound, on $U(Y)$ or, in the last row, on the function $\Phi $ of the proof of \cref {thm:cap-inequality}, which has to lie below the number on the right. For \cref {thm:count30,prop:C-radial} the value is the largest over the cases of the proof}{table.1}{}}
