\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Where $\varepsilon _0=4\cdot 10^{-26}$ comes from. (a) The chain of explicit bounds that replaces the compactness argument of \cref  {thm:near-contact}, with the number each step produces. Twenty-four directions with inner products at most $\tfrac  12+\kappa $ make every sign-changing sum-of-squares term of the certificate at least $-E$ in total (\cref  {thm:m24-robust}); so $\sigma _2\le E$ at each inner product up to $\tfrac  12$, which pins it near a zero of $\sigma _2$; \cref  {lem:root-lattice-robust} turns that into a distance from the root system; the rigidity of \cref  {thm:local-uniqueness}, with slack, bounds the displacement by the sum $S$ of the distances beyond contact; and the facet, moment and hull estimates close the argument. (b) To scale: the lower bound $2.62\cdot 10^{-4}f(u)$ of $\sigma _2$ near its double zero $u=0$, for $u>0$ and $u<0$, against the level $E(24,\kappa )=2.35\cdot 10^{-12}$. The two cross at $|u|\approx 2.7\cdot 10^{-4}$, inside the window $|u|\le \delta =3\cdot 10^{-4}$, where the bound is already $2.94\cdot 10^{-12}$. The other double zero, $-\tfrac  12$, gives the same picture; at the simple zeros $-1$ and $\tfrac  12$ the bound is linear and the window is far wider than needed.}}{78}{figure.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tikz-eps0}{{22}{78}{Where $\varepsilon _0=4\cdot 10^{-26}$ comes from. (a) The chain of explicit bounds that replaces the compactness argument of \cref {thm:near-contact}, with the number each step produces. Twenty-four directions with inner products at most $\tfrac 12+\kappa $ make every sign-changing sum-of-squares term of the certificate at least $-E$ in total (\cref {thm:m24-robust}); so $\sigma _2\le E$ at each inner product up to $\tfrac 12$, which pins it near a zero of $\sigma _2$; \cref {lem:root-lattice-robust} turns that into a distance from the root system; the rigidity of \cref {thm:local-uniqueness}, with slack, bounds the displacement by the sum $S$ of the distances beyond contact; and the facet, moment and hull estimates close the argument. (b) To scale: the lower bound $2.62\cdot 10^{-4}f(u)$ of $\sigma _2$ near its double zero $u=0$, for $u>0$ and $u<0$, against the level $E(24,\kappa )=2.35\cdot 10^{-12}$. The two cross at $|u|\approx 2.7\cdot 10^{-4}$, inside the window $|u|\le \delta =3\cdot 10^{-4}$, where the bound is already $2.94\cdot 10^{-12}$. The other double zero, $-\tfrac 12$, gives the same picture; at the simple zeros $-1$ and $\tfrac 12$ the bound is linear and the window is far wider than needed}{figure.22}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tikz-eps0@cref}{{[figure][22][]22}{[1][77][]78}}
