\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}{\ignorespaces (a) The section of the reference cell $\mathcal  {V}$, of $Q$, and of the cross-polytope $B$ by the plane spanned by the base direction $u_0$ and one transverse direction. Coordinates are exact: the section of $\mathcal  {V}$ is a hexagon, that of $Q$ the same hexagon with its right edge replaced by the two edges meeting at the apex $2u_0$, and that of $B$ a rhombus through the same apex and the same two vertices $\pm \sqrt  2\,v$. The dashed circle is the unit sphere, on which every contact hyperplane is tangent, and the shaded triangle is the section of the cap cut by a half-space at unit distance whose normal is tilted $30^\circ $ from $u_0$. (b) The volume of the cap cut from the cross-polytope by a half-space at unit distance, along three great circles leaving a vertex direction: towards an edge centre, towards a facet centre, and towards $\tfrac  12(1,1,1,1)$, where the half-space meets $B$ only in its four positive vertices and the cap volume falls to zero. The maximum $\tfrac  13$ of \cref  {thm:cap-inequality} is attained at the vertex direction, marked.}}{83}{figure.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cap}{{24}{83}{(a) The section of the reference cell $\mathcal {V}$, of $Q$, and of the cross-polytope $B$ by the plane spanned by the base direction $\base _0$ and one transverse direction. Coordinates are exact: the section of $\mathcal {V}$ is a hexagon, that of $Q$ the same hexagon with its right edge replaced by the two edges meeting at the apex $2\base _0$, and that of $B$ a rhombus through the same apex and the same two vertices $\pm \sqrt 2\,v$. The dashed circle is the unit sphere, on which every contact hyperplane is tangent, and the shaded triangle is the section of the cap cut by a half-space at unit distance whose normal is tilted $30^\circ $ from $\base _0$. (b) The volume of the cap cut from the cross-polytope by a half-space at unit distance, along three great circles leaving a vertex direction: towards an edge centre, towards a facet centre, and towards $\tfrac 12(1,1,1,1)$, where the half-space meets $B$ only in its four positive vertices and the cap volume falls to zero. The maximum $\tfrac 13$ of \cref {thm:cap-inequality} is attained at the vertex direction, marked}{figure.24}{}}
