\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {27}{\ignorespaces Neighbours that do not touch. (a) A two-dimensional section, to scale: two centres at distance $2.4$ from the central one and $2$ from each other, a packing; pulled in to distance $2$ they overlap (shaded), so the configuration at the all-contact corner is not a packing, and \cref  {lem:radial-new} gives a lower bound and not a contact configuration. (b) The distance criterion of \cref  {prop:distance-criterion} for $m$ contacts and $k$ further centres at a common distance $d$; it passes $8$ at the thresholds of \cref  {tab:distance-thresholds} (dots). (c) The remaining case is tight: the volume $\tfrac  {25}3-\tfrac  13(1-\tfrac  \delta 2)^4$ of the cell of the deletion of a root with one further centre at distance $2+\delta $ on the deleted root's axis, which tends to $8$ as $\delta \to 0$, and the least volume found by local minimisation from $60$ starts with one neighbour held at distance $2+\delta $. None is below $8$.}}{92}{figure.27}\protected@file@percent }
