\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {44}{\ignorespaces (a) The fundamental triangle of \cref  {lem:two-symmetries-new} on the sphere of deviation directions, with vertices $v_1,w_1,v_2$. The stabiliser of $u_0$ in $W(D_4)$ carries it to the eight octants. The reflections $S$ and $H$, through the dashed great circles, generate the group $S_3$ of \cref  {lem:s3-symmetry}, which permutes the vertices and the edges; the six small triangles cut out by the three dashed circles are the images of one of them. (b) The first arc in the plane of tilt $\varphi $ and arc position $s$, to scale: the breakpoint curves of \cref  {thm:arc1-breakpoints-new} and the eight regions they bound, shaded by the certificate of \cref  {thm:arc1-certs-new} that each carries. By \cref  {prop:arc2-is-arc1,prop:third-edge-cert} the same picture holds on the other two edges. The interior of the triangle is settled by \cref  {thm:eperp-closed}.}}{142}{figure.44}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fundamental-domain}{{44}{142}{(a) The fundamental triangle of \cref {lem:two-symmetries-new} on the sphere of deviation directions, with vertices $v_1,w_1,v_2$. The stabiliser of $u_0$ in $W(D_4)$ carries it to the eight octants. The reflections $S$ and $H$, through the dashed great circles, generate the group $S_3$ of \cref {lem:s3-symmetry}, which permutes the vertices and the edges; the six small triangles cut out by the three dashed circles are the images of one of them. (b) The first arc in the plane of tilt $\tilt $ and arc position $\arcp $, to scale: the breakpoint curves of \cref {thm:arc1-breakpoints-new} and the eight regions they bound, shaded by the certificate of \cref {thm:arc1-certs-new} that each carries. By \cref {prop:arc2-is-arc1,prop:third-edge-cert} the same picture holds on the other two edges. The interior of the triangle is settled by \cref {thm:eperp-closed}}{figure.44}{}}
\newlabel{fig:fundamental-domain@cref}{{[figure][44][2147483647]44}{[1][141][]142}}
